  INTRO

    Basically, you're this explorer stuck in a maze(14x30 on the first 
level, 14x62 or so otherwise,) and your objective is to gather keys to 
unlock doors to get to the treasure at the end of the level, and the 
more side treasures you pick up on the way and the quicker you finish, 
the more points you get.  Three kinds of monsters appear on specified 
squares and chase after you as you run through the maze.  You have one 
"smart bomb" (destroys all monsters) on the screen per life--it doesn't 
roll over, so the answer to "what time will I use it?" is "too early" or 
"too late"--and you can fire horizontally, although if you time things 
right that shot can knock out a monster just above/below you.  What's 
most frustrating is that you can't stop your man in the middle of a 
hallway, so you need to run into a wall to position yourself, as 
otherwise it's a bit tricky to run back and forth.  There are four 
cycling levels that increase in difficulty, as for each level you seem 
to need to go further back and forth in the maze with each level--you 
can only carry one key at a time, although each key can open any lock.  
After the first cycle you must pick up an additional key in each level.  
You have a Defender-like view at the top of the screen of where you are 
in the maze and where monsters are.  It's neat but too distracting to be 
useful.

