    It's a bit tougher here.  You can sneak in and get the first 
treasure, but beware here of using the portal below it as you may run 
into a monster when you come out.  You might even want to pass by the 
place that produces monsters to get to the first key--getting the second 
treasure will not be bad then.    From there use the teleporter back and 
skirt the lower wall.  Go up and note if you go all the way left, then 
down and left and right, you'll have stopped at a critical spot where 
you can pick off monsters coming from the right.  You may want to make a 
side trip to pick up the treasure just below it first, but be sure no 
monsters are too close to you when you go down.  The nice thing about 
reaching the rightmost treasure not in the open area is that if there 
are a lot of monsters below, you can fake them out by going through the 
teleporter.  Going up the passage before the first lock is tricky.  Use 
the niches to fire at monsters that are chasing you.  After you've 
unlocked the door beware that you won't be able to stop yourself and 
ambush the monsters, and don't go into the open spaces.  It'll take 
patience to get back down again, but use the niches and you'll make it.  
The other key isn't too hard to get if you use the middle teleporters.  
The open area is the toughest part, and the apple core looking things 
that come at you(butterflies?  Bats?)  are the toughest to shoot as they 
zigzag toward you, so a horizontal shot may miss them.  Wait until they 
are two or three squares away and lined up with you before shooting, or 
you may be frustrated.  It's possible to get the treasures and in fact 
for the rightmost one, you may want to go a square right and then up.  
If monsters are on your tail it'll be easier to pick them off firing to 
the left because they can't zigzag.

