    If you run right for the first treasure(right, up, right, through 
transporter, down, right, up, right) you'll get it.  Otherwise, you'll 
have some snakes to shoot through.  For picking up the key I recommend 
running up when you're below the transport--you'll have a solid place to 
stay and snipe a path to the key.  Getting out is a bit easier as you 
have several ways to do so.  After you see the second key(which you 
can't pick up) there is a long vertical passage with only one wall in 
the center.  If you wait and run down into the wall just to the left of 
the passage, you can snipe for a bit until the monster activity dies 
down.  You may have to time some 60-point monsters, but you can always 
run left into the wall below the pillar in the center if you hear a 
monster being produced.  It's not the worst idea to use a smart bomb 
here.  Once you do, it's not hard to get the three treasures to the 
right.  What is hard is dodging the two monster making areas, which may 
be an even better place to use the bomb.  The final treasure is a nice 
niche for shooting monsters before you go to unlock the first gate.  
Going back is a lot easier than coming in, but you'll have to run the 
gauntlet again.

