    Use the transporter to pick up the first key before the monster 
population gets dense.  You'll probably get the first treasure just 
walking by to the second set of transporters, and the second treasure 
will fall, too.  A lot of vigilance is required here due to the 
proliferation of vertical corridors.  If you pass by the top of the 
third set of transporters, take the zigzag path down as that will allow 
more chance to shoot horizontally.  You might as well pick up the fourth 
treasure as you can shoot from the niche.  The corridor is lousy with 
monsters, but you might as well pick up the fifth treasure, too, as 
there are no places near that will make monsters.  From there more up-
down stuff and if you want to take the sixth treasure run into the wall 
two squares above the final monster spawning pit if monsters are around 
or being created.  Don't run unless a monster comes from up top.  Then 
motor in to unlock the gate, and you'll get to go back(tougher than in 
level 3) and return.  Your reward is an even tougher version of level 1.

  MISCELLANEOUS

--I think it's possible to smart-bomb and still get killed, if there are 
a lot of monsters on the screen and one is really close to you.

